# Host Composition

Use this pattern for `LTs.Soong.Host` and future runnable host projects.

## Program

- Use an explicit `Program` class with `Main`.
- Wrap startup in `try/catch`, resolve `ILogger<Program>` from the Autofac root, and log startup failures.
- For Web APIs, call `ConfigureDefaultHostApplication<Program>` on `WebApplication.CreateBuilder( args )`.
- Keep `Program` as the composition root only. Do not put business logic in `Program`.
- Put configuration registration in `Program.RegisterConfiguration( ContainerBuilder builder )`.
- Never create a separate `ConfigurationIoC.cs` or other configuration bootstrap class.
- Use `internal static` or `protected static` methods on `Program` for configuration and service registration when tests need access.

```csharp
private static void Main( string[] args )
{
    ILogger? logger = null;

    try
    {
        var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder( args );

        builder.ConfigureDefaultHostApplication<Program>(
            string.Empty,
            RegisterConfiguration,
            RegisterServices,
            RegisterWebServices );

        var app = builder.Build();

        var container = app.Services.GetAutofacRoot();
        logger = container.Resolve<ILogger<Program>>();

        ConfigurePipeline( app );

        app.Run();
    }
    catch( Exception ex )
    {
        logger?.LogError( ex, "An error occurred while starting the application" );
        throw;
    }
}

internal static void RegisterConfiguration( ContainerBuilder builder )
{
    builder.RegisterLogConfiguration( "Logging:Files" );
    builder.AddSoongHostConfiguration( SoongHostConfiguration.SectionName );
    builder.AddOllamaConfiguration( OllamaConfiguration.SectionName );
}
```

## Configuration

- Follow `.cursor/rules/configuration.mdc` for typed configuration records, loaders, and appsettings layout.
- Chain all host configuration registration inside `Program.RegisterConfiguration`.
- Pass `RegisterConfiguration` directly to `ConfigureDefaultHostApplication`.

## Dependency Injection

- Use Autofac extension methods in `DependencyInjection/` for service registration.
- Name service registration entry points `Add<Area>...`.
- Register runtime singletons in Autofac, not ad hoc MS.DI registrations in `Program`.
- Use `IAutofacConfigurationProvider.Get<T>()` inside service registration when typed configuration is required.

## Web API

- Register controllers in `Program.RegisterWebServices( IServiceCollection services )` with `services.AddControllers()`.
- Map controllers in `ConfigurePipeline` with `app.MapControllers()`.
- Place HTTP endpoints in `Controllers/`, not minimal API `Endpoints/` classes.

## Project Layout

- `Program.cs` at the host project root.
- `Configuration/` for configuration types and loaders only.
- `DependencyInjection/` for Autofac service registration extensions.
- `Controllers/` for API controllers.
- `Functions/` for Azure Function trigger entry points when applicable.
- `Composition/` for factories and runtime wiring shared by the host.
- Keep domain behavior in sibling projects; the host project composes them.

## Packages

- Use `LTs.Hosting` for `ConfigureDefaultHostApplication`.
- Use `LTs.Logging` for Serilog registration helpers.
- Use `LTs.Configurations` for default configuration loading.
- Use `LTs.DependencyInjections` for `GetAutofacRoot`.
